## 7. Functional Requirements

> **Hybrid Analyst Note:** All functional requirements are explicitly mapped to underlying data entities and analytical outputs to ensure traceability between business rules, SQL logic, and BI reporting.

### 7.1 Leasing Management

* The system shall allow creation, modification, and termination of leases
* Each lease shall be linked to a unique Customer ID and VIN
* Lease start and end dates shall be mandatory

### 7.2 Inventory Management

* The system shall display real-time vehicle availability
* Vehicles assigned to active leases shall be marked unavailable
* Double-booking of vehicles shall be prevented

### 7.3 Payment Tracking

* The system shall track payments against each lease
* Late payments shall be automatically identified
* Late fees shall be calculated based on predefined rules

### 7.4 Dispute Management

* Customers shall be able to submit formal dispute notices
* Disputes shall be linked to specific payments and leases
* Dispute status and resolution history shall be auditable

### 7.5 Reporting & Analytics

* The system shall identify revenue at risk from overdue leases using SQL-driven date-difference logic
* Dashboards shall display inventory utilization, lease aging, and delinquency trends
* Metrics shall be validated directly against source tables (Leases, Payments, Vehicles)
* Analytical outputs shall support both operational monitoring and executive decision-making
* The system shall identify revenue at risk from overdue leases
* Dashboards shall display inventory utilization
* Reports shall support operational and management decision-making

---

## 8. Non-Functional Requirements

### 8.1 Performance

* Inventory and lease status updates shall be near real time
* Standard queries shall return results within acceptable response times

### 8.2 Data Integrity & Security

* Enforced primary and foreign key relationships
* Validation of data types for monetary and date fields
* Controlled access based on user roles

### 8.3 Scalability

* The database design shall support future growth in customers, vehicles, and leases

---

## 9. Data Requirements

> **Hybrid Analyst Ownership:** Data requirements are defined to support operational workflows *and* downstream analytics, ensuring a single source of truth across the system.

### 9.1 Core Entities

* Customers
* Vehicles
* Leases
* Payments

### 9.2 Key Data Attributes

* Unique identifiers (Customer ID, Lease ID, Payment ID)
* VIN for vehicle tracking
* Date fields for lease terms
* Decimal fields for payment and fee amounts

---

## 10. Assumptions & Constraints

### Analyst Assumptions

* Business rules will be enforced primarily through data logic rather than manual status flags
* Date-based calculations will be preferred to ensure analytical flexibility and accuracy

### Constraints

### 10.1 Assumptions

* Users will transition from Excel-based workflows
* Data migration from legacy spreadsheets will be feasible

### 10.2 Constraints

* Solution must align with SQL Server standards
* Budget and timeline constraints limit initial feature scope

---

## 11. Acceptance Criteria

> Acceptance criteria validate not only functional correctness, but also **data accuracy and analytical reliability**.

* All core leasing and payment workflows function end to end
* Automated identification of overdue leases is accurate
* Reports correctly identify revenue at risk
* UAT scripts pass for both happy path and edge case scenarios

